    <md:title>Unit 7 Overview and Readiness</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b50563db-efb6-444d-b65a-10b7fc56424f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this unit, students will:</para>
<list>
  <item>Identify quadratic functions from expressions, tables, and graphs.</item>
  <item>Represent quadratic equations in standard and factored form.</item>
  <item>Graph quadratic equations from standard form, factored form, and vertex form.</item>
  <item>Describe how the \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) in \(ax^2 + bx + c\) affect the graph of a quadratic equation.</item>
  <item>Determine whether a visual pattern represents a linear, exponential, or quadratic relationship.</item>
</list>
<para>To accomplish these unit-level learning goals, students will complete the following lessons and activities.</para>
<title>Student Readiness for Unit 7</title>
<para>To be ready for this unit, students will need to be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Multiply binomials.</item>
  <item>Factor trinomials.</item>
  <item>Compare linear and exponential functions.</item>
</list>
<para>This Unit Overview Video will provide a big picture look at the content found in this unit as well as the prerequisite skills that students need for accessing the content in the unit.</para>

<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/kVYNdK3ljZc;&amp;rel=0"/></media><div class="os-raise-accordion">
